## Django Settings Configuration

### Core Dependencies

- Django==4.2.20
- Django REST Framework==3.14.0 (for API development)
- Celery==5.5.2 (for background tasks)
- Redis==5.2.1 (for caching and task queues)
- MySQL (mysqlclient==2.2.4) as production database
- Channels==4.2.2 (for WebSocket support)
- Daphne==4.1.2 (ASGI server)

### Additional Dependencies

- django-cors-headers==4.3.1 (CORS handling)
- django-environ==0.10.0 (environment management)
- django-extensions==4.0 (development utilities)
- django-filter==25.1 (filtering)
- djangorestframework-simplejwt==5.3.1 (JWT authentication)
- drf-spectacular==0.26.5 (API documentation)
- whitenoise==6.6.0 (static file serving)
- django-redis==6.0.0 (Redis cache backend)

### Environment Configuration

- Use django-environ for environment variable management
- Store sensitive data in .env file (not in version control)
- Configure database settings via environment variables
- Set DEBUG=False in production
- Use Asia/Seoul timezone

### Security Settings

- Configure CORS properly for frontend integration
- Use whitenoise for static file serving
- Implement proper CSRF protection
- Configure JWT token settings
  

